import Scc.Cert.Rt.CodeA64
import Scc.Cert.LinkA64
import Scc.Cert.Rt.WideA64
import Scc.Cert.Rt.A64Abort
import Scc.Cert.NeedA64

/-!
# Every block of `hello.w`'s AArch64 code at its place

Generated by `scc --code`. `helloProg` and `helloSecs` are the program and
the data sections the canonical loader reads from the listing `helloAsm`
(`Scc.Sem.A64.textProgram`, `Scc.Sem.dataSections`, at elaboration time); the
kernel cannot run the parsers, so these two equations are the trust boundary,
checked by evaluation (`#guard`).

Per function, the table of its `block_spec` blocks (`scc --blocks`, named in
comments), grouped by the label before them with their instruction counts
from it, in program order; `helloT_in` checks them all against `helloProg` by
`kernel_rfl` (`blocksIn`, `Scc/Cert/Rt/CodeA64.lean`): every block is code
at its label and offset in every layout of the program
(`codeAt_of_blocksIn`), the loaded thread's included (`lays_threadAt`).

`helloΛ` is the layout of the program's static link (`Scc.Cert.Link`),
with the program's immediate table `helloImms` when stated (`Layout.imms`):
`helloΛ_wf` its well-formedness, `helloΛ_aborts` its abort labels in the
program, `helloΛ_image` each data symbol's item in its image
(`Scc.Cert.Link.image_symbols`), `helloΛ_load` the canonical loader's checks
of it (but the entry state's), with a valid layout of the loaded thread
(`validLayout_of_loadOk`). `hello_wide`, if stated, puts the program in the
one-word fragment (`Scc.Cert.WideA64.wideIn`), so its certification
semantics writes words only (`wideSt_threadAt`). `hello_abort` checks the
abort stubs and `scc_rt_abort`, `hello_print` `scc_rt_print`
(`Scc/Cert/Rt/A64Print.lean`), and `hello_mainTail`, when stated (the
listing has it in a shape Spike proves), the tail of `scc_rt_main`: the
code the runtime's proofs take as hypotheses (`Scc/Cert/Rt/A64Abort.lean`);
`hello_printL`, when stated, `wc_printL`'s (`Scc/Cert/Rt/A64PrintL.lean`).
`helloNeed`, if stated, is
the stack need of its stack-checked functions, checked on `helloProg`
(`helloNeed_ok`, `Scc/Cert/NeedA64.lean`).
-/

namespace SccCode

